# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sample-based Krylov Quantum Diagonalization ([SKQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.09702)) is a quantum-centric variant of subspace diagonalization. Rather than sampling a single variational ansatz (as in plain sample-based quantum diagonalization ([SQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.05068))) or an ensemble of randomized time-evolution circuits (as in [SqDRIFT](sqdrift#sqdrift-getting-started)), it samples a *Krylov* basis: the family of states\n"
msgstr "Ang Sample-based Krylov Quantum Diagonalization ([SKQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.09702)) ay isang quantum-centric na variant ng subspace diagonalization. Sa halip na mag-sample ng iisang variational ansatz (tulad ng sa payak na sample-based quantum diagonalization ([SQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.05068))) o ng ensemble ng mga randomized na time-evolution circuit (tulad ng sa [SqDRIFT](sqdrift#sqdrift-getting-started)), nagsa-sample ito ng *Krylov* basis: ang pamilya ng mga state\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\lvert \\psi_k \\rangle = e^{-i k \\, \\Delta t \\, H} \\lvert \\psi_0 \\rangle, \\qquad k = 0, 1, \\dots,\n"
"D - 1,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\lvert \\psi_k \\rangle = e^{-i k \\, \\Delta t \\, H} \\lvert \\psi_0 \\rangle, \\qquad k = 0, 1, \\dots,\n"
"D - 1,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "obtained by evolving a reference state $\\lvert \\psi_0 \\rangle$ for increasing multiples of a fixed time step $\\Delta t$. Bitstrings sampled from these $D$ circuits populate the Krylov subspace in which the Hamiltonian is subsequently diagonalized classically.\n"
msgstr "na nakukuha sa pag-evolve ng isang reference state $\\lvert \\psi_0 \\rangle$ para sa pataas na multiple ng isang nakapirming time step $\\Delta t$. Ang mga bitstring na na-sample mula sa $D$ circuit na ito ay bumubuo sa Krylov subspace kung saan idi-diagonalize nang klasikal ang Hamiltonian pagkatapos.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide reproduces the circuit-construction step of the [SKQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.09702) algorithm for the single-impurity Anderson model (SIAM), a magnetic impurity coupled to a non-interacting bath, following the [SKQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.09702) publication.\n"
msgstr "Ginagaya ng gabay na ito ang hakbang ng pagbuo ng circuit ng algorithm na [SKQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.09702) para sa single-impurity Anderson model (SIAM), isang magnetic impurity na nakakabit sa isang non-interacting na bath, kasunod ng publikasyon ng [SKQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.09702).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The SKQD sampling step works only if the ground state is **sparse** in the computational basis: the classical diagonalization must be able to reconstruct it from a manageable number of sampled bitstrings. As shown below, that sparsity is not automatic; it is a property of the single-particle basis in which the problem is expressed. Getting the basis right is the crux of this construction.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Gumagana lang ang hakbang ng sampling ng SKQD kung **sparse** ang ground state sa computational basis: dapat kayang buuin ng klasikal na diagonalization ito mula sa kakayanin na bilang ng mga na-sample na bitstring. Tulad ng makikita sa ibaba, hindi awtomatiko ang sparsity na iyon; katangian ito ng single-particle basis kung saan ipinahayag ang problema. Ang pagpili ng tamang basis ang pinakapuso ng konstruksiyong ito.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"build-the-siam-hamiltonian-as-a-fermionic-operator\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Build the SIAM Hamiltonian as a fermionic operator {#1-build-the-siam-hamiltonian-as-a-fermionic-operator}"
msgstr "1. Buuin ang SIAM Hamiltonian bilang fermionic operator {#1-build-the-siam-hamiltonian-as-a-fermionic-operator}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The single-impurity Anderson model places one interacting impurity orbital (index $0$) in contact with a non-interacting bath of $L$ sites arranged as a chain. Its Hamiltonian splits into a one-body part $H_1$ and a two-body part $H_2$,\n"
msgstr "Naglalagay ang single-impurity Anderson model ng isang interacting na impurity orbital (index $0$) na nakadikit sa isang non-interacting na bath na may $L$ na site na nakaayos bilang chain. Nahahati ang Hamiltonian nito sa isang one-body na bahagi na $H_1$ at isang two-body na bahagi na $H_2$,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = H_1 + H_2,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = H_1 + H_2,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "with the one-body part collecting the impurity on-site energy (the chemical potential $\\mu$), the impurity–bath hybridization $V$, and the nearest-neighbor bath hopping $t$,\n"
msgstr "kung saan kinokolekta ng one-body na bahagi ang on-site energy ng impurity (ang chemical potential na $\\mu$), ang impurity–bath hybridization na $V$, at ang nearest-neighbor na bath hopping na $t$,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H_1 = \\mu \\sum_\\sigma a^\\dagger_{0\\sigma} a_{0\\sigma}\n"
"      - V \\sum_\\sigma \\left( a^\\dagger_{0\\sigma} a_{1\\sigma} + \\text{h.c.} \\right)\n"
"      - t \\sum_{\\sigma} \\sum_{i=1}^{L-1}\n"
"        \\left( a^\\dagger_{i\\sigma} a_{i+1,\\sigma} + \\text{h.c.} \\right),\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H_1 = \\mu \\sum_\\sigma a^\\dagger_{0\\sigma} a_{0\\sigma}\n"
"      - V \\sum_\\sigma \\left( a^\\dagger_{0\\sigma} a_{1\\sigma} + \\text{h.c.} \\right)\n"
"      - t \\sum_{\\sigma} \\sum_{i=1}^{L-1}\n"
"        \\left( a^\\dagger_{i\\sigma} a_{i+1,\\sigma} + \\text{h.c.} \\right),\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and the two-body part carrying the on-site Coulomb repulsion $U$ on the impurity alone,\n"
msgstr "at dala ng two-body na bahagi ang on-site na Coulomb repulsion na $U$ sa impurity lang,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H_2 = U \\, a^\\dagger_{0\\uparrow} a_{0\\uparrow} a^\\dagger_{0\\downarrow} a_{0\\downarrow}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H_2 = U \\, a^\\dagger_{0\\uparrow} a_{0\\uparrow} a^\\dagger_{0\\downarrow} a_{0\\downarrow}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide works at the particle-hole-symmetric point $\\mu = -U/2$. These two parts map directly onto the one-body integrals `h1e` (bath hopping, impurity hybridization, impurity on-site energy) and the single two-body integral `h2e` (the impurity Coulomb term). First assemble them in the position basis, where the model is naturally defined.\n"
msgstr "Gumagana ang gabay na ito sa particle-hole-symmetric na punto na $\\mu = -U/2$. Direktang nagma-map ang dalawang bahaging ito sa mga one-body integral na `h1e` (bath hopping, impurity hybridization, impurity on-site energy) at sa nag-iisang two-body integral na `h2e` (ang Coulomb term ng impurity). Buuin muna ang mga ito sa position basis, kung saan natural na tinutukoy ang model.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"change-to-the-momentum-basis\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Change to the momentum basis {#2-change-to-the-momentum-basis}"
msgstr "2. Lumipat sa momentum basis {#2-change-to-the-momentum-basis}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The bath part of the SIAM is a free-fermion chain, so it is diagonalized by a change to the momentum basis. This is the decisive step for SKQD. Because the bath is translationally invariant, the ground state is not sparse in the position basis, but it is sparse in the momentum basis, where the bath Hamiltonian is diagonal. The single-particle orbital rotation that performs this change is problem-specific linear algebra. It diagonalizes the bath hopping matrix while leaving the impurity orbital untouched, then relocates the impurity to a central site:\n"
msgstr "Ang bahagi ng bath ng SIAM ay isang free-fermion chain, kaya dina-diagonalize ito ng paglipat sa momentum basis. Ito ang mapagpasyang hakbang para sa SKQD. Dahil translationally invariant ang bath, hindi sparse ang ground state sa position basis, pero sparse ito sa momentum basis, kung saan diagonal ang Hamiltonian ng bath. Ang single-particle orbital rotation na gumagawa ng paglipat na ito ay linear algebra na partikular sa problema. Dina-diagonalize nito ang bath hopping matrix habang hindi ginagalaw ang impurity orbital, saka inililipat ang impurity sa isang sentral na site:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unlike a variational workflow, this rotates the Hamiltonian integrals into the momentum basis, so that the whole circuit (Hamiltonian and state alike) lives in the basis where the ground state is sparse and the sampled bitstrings are therefore informative. Rotating the one- and two-body integrals is a standard basis change of the electronic-structure tensors:\n"
msgstr "Hindi tulad ng variational workflow, ina-rotate nito ang mga Hamiltonian integral papunta sa momentum basis, para ang buong circuit (Hamiltonian at state pareho) ay nasa basis kung saan sparse ang ground state at kaya may saysay ang mga na-sample na bitstring. Ang pag-rotate ng mga one- at two-body integral ay isang karaniwang basis change ng mga tensor ng electronic-structure:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because the rotation leaves the impurity orbital fixed (it acts only on the bath), the on-site interaction is unchanged. `h2e_momentum` remains a single number-number term, just like `h2e`. The only change is that the impurity has been relocated to a central index. This is visible directly in the integral tensors, which each carry one nonzero entry:\n"
msgstr "Dahil hindi ginagalaw ng rotation ang impurity orbital (sa bath lang ito kumikilos), hindi nagbabago ang on-site na interaksiyon. Nananatiling iisang number-number term ang `h2e_momentum`, tulad ng `h2e`. Ang tanging pagbabago ay nailipat ang impurity sa isang sentral na index. Kitang-kita ito mismo sa mga integral tensor, na bawat isa ay may isang nonzero na entry:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This locality is what keeps the interaction cheap to synthesize later.\n"
msgstr "Ang lokalidad na ito ang nagpapanatiling mura ang pag-synthesize ng interaksiyon sa bandang huli.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Assemble the one-body integrals into a [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") with the electronic-integral constructor [`from_1body_tril_spin_sym()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator.from_1body_tril_spin_sym \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator.from_1body_tril_spin_sym\"), which expects them packed into lower-triangular ordering. The two-body part is a single number-number term, so rather than routing it through the two-body integral machinery, build it directly with [`cre()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-cre#qiskit_fermions.operators.cre \"qiskit_fermions.operators.cre\")/[`ann()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-ann#qiskit_fermions.operators.ann \"qiskit_fermions.operators.ann\"): the on-site Coulomb operator $U \\, n_{p\\uparrow} n_{p\\downarrow}$ for the impurity mode $p$ (its $\\uparrow$ mode at index `p`, its $\\downarrow$ mode at index `p + norb` in the block-spin layout). Both constructors spin-double the `norb` spatial orbitals into `2 * norb` fermionic modes.\n"
msgstr "I-assemble ang mga one-body integral sa isang [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") gamit ang constructor ng electronic-integral na [`from_1body_tril_spin_sym()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator.from_1body_tril_spin_sym \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator.from_1body_tril_spin_sym\"), na umaasang naka-pack ang mga ito sa lower-triangular na ordering. Iisang number-number term ang two-body na bahagi, kaya sa halip na idaan ito sa makinarya ng two-body integral, buuin ito nang direkta gamit ang [`cre()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-cre#qiskit_fermions.operators.cre \"qiskit_fermions.operators.cre\")/[`ann()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-ann#qiskit_fermions.operators.ann \"qiskit_fermions.operators.ann\"): ang on-site na Coulomb operator na $U \\, n_{p\\uparrow} n_{p\\downarrow}$ para sa impurity mode na $p$ (ang $\\uparrow$ mode nito sa index na `p`, ang $\\downarrow$ mode nito sa index na `p + norb` sa block-spin na layout). Dinodoble ng parehong constructor ang spin ng `norb` na spatial orbital papunta sa `2 * norb` na fermionic mode.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keep the one-body part $H_1$ and the two-body part $H_2$ as separate operators rather than summing them eagerly, matching the terms $H_1$ and $H_2$ of the section-1 equations. Building each piece once (in both bases) makes them reusable below. Summed, they give the full Hamiltonian for the exact diagonalization in either basis. Individually, $H_2$ (momentum basis) is the operator the Trotter step evolves in step 4.\n"
msgstr "Panatilihing magkahiwalay na operator ang one-body na bahagi na $H_1$ at ang two-body na bahagi na $H_2$ sa halip na pagsamahin agad ang mga ito, ayon sa mga term na $H_1$ at $H_2$ ng mga equation sa seksyon 1. Dahil minsan mo lang bubuuin ang bawat piraso (sa parehong basis), magagamit mo itong muli sa ibaba. Kapag pinagsama, ibibigay nila ang buong Hamiltonian para sa exact diagonalization sa alinmang basis. Nang magkahiwalay, ang $H_2$ (momentum basis) ang operator na ine-evolve ng Trotter step sa hakbang 4.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The basis change is a unitary similarity transform, so it leaves the spectrum untouched. Confirm the operator is correct by comparing its lowest eigenvalue in the $(\\text{norb}, \\text{nelec})$ sector against an exact diagonalization. The [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") exposes a SciPy [`LinearOperator`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\") (backed by a native full configuration interaction (FCI) matrix-vector kernel), so it can be handed straight to [`scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh()`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\").\n"
msgstr "Ang basis change ay isang unitary similarity transform, kaya hindi nito ginagalaw ang spectrum. Tiyaking tama ang operator sa pamamagitan ng paghahambing ng pinakamababang eigenvalue nito sa sector na $(\\text{norb}, \\text{nelec})$ laban sa exact diagonalization. Nagbibigay ang [`FermionOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-fermion-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.FermionOperator\") ng SciPy [`LinearOperator`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.LinearOperator \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\") (na suportado ng native na full configuration interaction (FCI) matrix-vector kernel), kaya puwede itong ipasa nang diretso sa [`scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh()`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\").\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The payoff of the basis change is sparsity. To make it concrete, count how many computational-basis determinants are needed to capture 99% of the ground-state weight, and compare the momentum basis against the position basis. The energy is basis-independent, but the number of determinants is not:\n"
msgstr "Ang pakinabang ng basis change ay ang sparsity. Para gawin itong konkreto, bilangin kung ilang computational-basis determinant ang kailangan para makuha ang 99% ng bigat ng ground state, at ihambing ang momentum basis sa position basis. Hindi nakadepende sa basis ang energy, pero ang bilang ng mga determinant ay oo:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two operators share the same energy, but the position-basis ground state is spread over thousands of determinants, while the momentum basis concentrates it onto around 20, which is why SKQD sampling works in the momentum basis and not the position basis.\n"
msgstr "Magkapareho ang energy ng dalawang operator, pero nakakalat ang ground state sa position basis sa libu-libong determinant, habang pinagsisiksik ito ng momentum basis sa humigit-kumulang 20, kaya gumagana ang SKQD sampling sa momentum basis at hindi sa position basis.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"prepare-the-reference-state\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Prepare the reference state {#3-prepare-the-reference-state}"
msgstr "3. Ihanda ang reference state {#3-prepare-the-reference-state}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The SKQD reference $\\lvert \\psi_0 \\rangle$ is the superposition of all excitations of the electrons closest to the Fermi level into the nearest empty momentum modes. The [SKQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.09702) publication builds it with a hand-written network of [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate)s. It looks strongly correlated (it has hundreds of nonzero computational-basis amplitudes), but a network of number-conserving two-mode rotations is a single-particle (fermionic Gaussian) operation, so the state it produces is a single Slater determinant. That means you can prepare it with one [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") gate, given the single-particle rotation the network implements.\n"
msgstr "Ang SKQD reference na $\\lvert \\psi_0 \\rangle$ ay ang superposition ng lahat ng excitation ng mga electron na pinakamalapit sa Fermi level papunta sa pinakamalapit na walang lamang momentum mode. Binubuo ito ng publikasyon ng [SKQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.09702) gamit ang isang kamay na isinulat na network ng mga [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate). Mukha itong malakas ang correlation (mayroon itong daan-daang nonzero na computational-basis amplitude), pero ang network ng mga number-conserving na two-mode rotation ay isang single-particle (fermionic Gaussian) na operasyon, kaya ang state na nagagawa nito ay iisang Slater determinant. Ibig sabihin, maihahanda mo ito gamit ang isang [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") gate, kung ibibigay ang single-particle rotation na ipinatutupad ng network.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because each [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate) acts as a Givens rotation on a pair of modes, that rotation can be built directly in the single-particle picture (one Givens matrix per gate) instead of emitting the two-qubit gates by hand. The gates form a brickwork of nearest-neighbor rotations that fans out from the Fermi level in expanding layers, spreading each near-Fermi electron across the empty modes just above it:\n"
msgstr "Dahil kumikilos ang bawat [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate) bilang Givens rotation sa isang pares ng mode, maaaring buuin ang rotation na iyon nang direkta sa single-particle na pananaw (isang Givens matrix bawat gate) sa halip na isulat nang mano-mano ang mga two-qubit gate. Bumubuo ang mga gate ng brickwork ng mga nearest-neighbor na rotation na kumakalat mula sa Fermi level sa lumalawak na mga layer, na ikinakalat ang bawat electron na malapit sa Fermi sa mga walang lamang mode na nasa itaas lang nito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The rotation above is expressed in the momentum basis, matching the Hamiltonian. The electrons near the Fermi level are the highest-energy occupied momentum modes, and the network excites them into the lowest-energy empty ones. This is why the reference must be built after the basis change of the previous step, not before.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Ang rotation sa itaas ay ipinahayag sa momentum basis, na tugma sa Hamiltonian. Ang mga electron malapit sa Fermi level ay ang mga occupied na momentum mode na may pinakamataas na energy, at ine-excite sila ng network papunta sa mga walang lamang mode na may pinakamababang energy. Kaya dapat buuin ang reference pagkatapos ng basis change ng nakaraang hakbang, hindi bago nito.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Slater determinant preparation is done per spin sector, since each sector has its own (electrons, orbitals) shape. A single [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") gate (an occupation, the lowest `nocc` modes filled, together with the single-particle rotation) prepares one sector; the same gate is applied once on the alpha modes `0..norb` and once on the beta modes `norb..2*norb`, since both spin sectors share the same reference occupation and rotation here:\n"
msgstr "Ginagawa ang paghahanda ng Slater determinant kada spin sector, dahil may sarili nitong hugis (mga electron, mga orbital) ang bawat sector. Isang [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") gate (isang occupation, na pinunan ang pinakamababang `nocc` na mode, kasama ang single-particle rotation) ang naghahanda ng isang sector; ang parehong gate ay inilalapat nang isang beses sa mga alpha mode na `0..norb` at isang beses sa mga beta mode na `norb..2*norb`, dahil pareho ang reference occupation at rotation ng dalawang spin sector dito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This declarative gate replaces the hand-coded [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate) network; the transpiler generates the Givens-rotation synthesis.\n"
msgstr "Pinapalitan ng deklaratibong gate na ito ang kamay na isinulat na network ng [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate); ang transpiler ang bumubuo ng Givens-rotation synthesis.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"assemble-the-krylov-circuits\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Assemble the Krylov circuits {#4-assemble-the-krylov-circuits}"
msgstr "4. I-assemble ang mga Krylov circuit {#4-assemble-the-krylov-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each Krylov circuit is the reference-state preparation followed by evolution under $e^{-i k \\, \\Delta t \\, H}$. Split the Hamiltonian into its one-body and two-body parts, $H = H_1 + H_2$, and Trotterize the evolution over that split. This is the decisive choice for circuit depth. The one-body evolution $e^{-i t H_1}$ is a free-fermion (fermionic Gaussian) operation, so it is a single-particle basis rotation (an [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") with unitary $e^{-i t \\, \\mathbf{h}_1}$) rather than something that has to be Pauli-Trotterized term by term. The two-body evolution $e^{-i t H_2}$ acts only on the single on-site interaction term. Building the step this way lets the transpiler emit a shallow brickwork of Givens rotations plus a single two-qubit interaction gate, the shallow structure that the [SKQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.09702) publication builds by hand.\n"
msgstr "Ang bawat Krylov circuit ay ang paghahanda ng reference state na sinusundan ng evolution sa ilalim ng $e^{-i k \\, \\Delta t \\, H}$. Hatiin ang Hamiltonian sa one-body at two-body na bahagi nito, $H = H_1 + H_2$, at i-Trotterize ang evolution ayon sa paghahating iyon. Ito ang mapagpasyang pagpili para sa circuit depth. Ang one-body evolution na $e^{-i t H_1}$ ay isang free-fermion (fermionic Gaussian) na operasyon, kaya isa itong single-particle basis rotation (isang [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") na may unitary na $e^{-i t \\, \\mathbf{h}_1}$) at hindi isang bagay na kailangang i-Pauli-Trotterize bawat term. Ang two-body evolution na $e^{-i t H_2}$ ay kumikilos lang sa iisang on-site na interaction term. Dahil sa ganitong pagbuo ng step, makakapag-emit ang transpiler ng mababaw na brickwork ng mga Givens rotation kasama ang iisang two-qubit na interaction gate, ang mababaw na estrukturang binubuo nang mano-mano ng publikasyon ng [SKQD](https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.09702).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We already have the two-body part. It is the `two_body_momentum` operator built in step 2 (the single on-site term). The one-body evolution $e^{-i t H_1}$ is spin-independent, so it is a single per-sector [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") with unitary $e^{-i t \\, \\mathbf{h}_1}$ applied once to each spin sector, the same parallel structure as the reference-state preparation.\n"
msgstr "Mayroon na tayo ng two-body na bahagi. Ito ang operator na `two_body_momentum` na binuo sa hakbang 2 (ang iisang on-site na term). Hindi nakadepende sa spin ang one-body evolution na $e^{-i t H_1}$, kaya isa itong [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") kada sector na may unitary na $e^{-i t \\, \\mathbf{h}_1}$ na inilalapat nang isang beses sa bawat spin sector, na kapareho ng parallel na estruktura ng paghahanda ng reference state.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each Krylov circuit evolves for a total time $k \\, \\Delta t$. That is realized with a second-order Trotter product of $k$ steps of size $\\Delta t$, so the per-step error stays fixed as the Krylov dimension grows. Each step sandwiches a full one-body rotation (one per spin sector) between two half-steps of the (cheap, single-term) two-body evolution. The Krylov dimension $D$ is the number of such circuits, with `dim` ranging from `0` (reference state only) to $D - 1$.\n"
msgstr "Ang bawat Krylov circuit ay nag-e-evolve para sa kabuuang oras na $k \\, \\Delta t$. Natutupad ito sa pamamagitan ng second-order na Trotter product ng $k$ na hakbang na may laking $\\Delta t$, kaya nananatiling nakapirmi ang error kada hakbang habang lumalaki ang Krylov dimension. Naglalagay ang bawat hakbang ng buong one-body rotation (isa kada spin sector) sa pagitan ng dalawang kalahating hakbang ng (mura, iisang term na) two-body evolution. Ang Krylov dimension na $D$ ay ang bilang ng mga ganoong circuit, na ang `dim` ay mula `0` (reference state lang) hanggang $D - 1$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The circuits built here carry no measurements yet, because the same fermionic circuits also drive the exact simulation in step 6, and a measurement is not a unitary operation. Step 5 adds them with [`FermionicCircuit.measure_all()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all\"), which reads mode `i` into classical bit `i`.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Wala pang mga measurement ang mga circuit na binuo dito, dahil ang parehong mga fermionic circuit ang nagpapatakbo rin ng exact simulation sa hakbang 6, at hindi unitary na operasyon ang measurement. Idinaragdag ito ng hakbang 5 gamit ang [`FermionicCircuit.measure_all()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit.measure_all\"), na bumabasa ng mode `i` papunta sa classical bit `i`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Prefer measuring the *fermionic* circuit over the transpiled one. A fermionic measurement names the mode it reads, so layout and routing carry it along with the qubit that mode ended up on, and the sampled bitstring is indexed by mode. Measuring the transpiled circuit instead leaves you to undo [`final_index_layout()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.TranspileLayout#final_index_layout) yourself, and silently returns permuted results if you forget. This relies on the occupation-basis Jordan-Wigner encoding the preset uses, where each mode is carried by one qubit.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Mas mainam na sukatin ang *fermionic* na circuit kaysa sa na-transpile. Pinangangalanan ng fermionic na measurement ang mode na binabasa nito, kaya dala ito ng layout at routing kasama ang qubit na napuntahan ng mode na iyon, at naka-index ayon sa mode ang na-sample na bitstring. Kapag ang na-transpile na circuit ang sinukat, ikaw na ang kailangang mag-undo ng [`final_index_layout()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.TranspileLayout#final_index_layout), at tahimik itong magbabalik ng mga permuted na resulta kapag nakalimutan mo. Umaasa ito sa occupation-basis na Jordan-Wigner encoding na ginagamit ng preset, kung saan isang qubit ang may dala sa bawat mode.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"transpile-to-qubit-circuits\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. Transpile to qubit circuits {#5-transpile-to-qubit-circuits}"
msgstr "5. I-transpile sa mga qubit circuit {#5-transpile-to-qubit-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpiling a [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") maps its fermionic gates to qubit gates. This uses the Jordan-Wigner [`jordan_wigner()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-jordan-wigner#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner\") mapping. The [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") gates synthesize into a brickwork of Givens rotations, and the single-term [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") lowers to a single two-qubit interaction gate.\n"
msgstr "Ang pag-transpile ng isang [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") ay nagma-map sa mga fermionic gate nito papunta sa mga qubit gate. Gumagamit ito ng Jordan-Wigner na mapping na [`jordan_wigner()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-library-jordan-wigner#qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.library.jordan_wigner\"). Ang mga [`OrbitalRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-orbital-rotation#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.OrbitalRotation\") na gate ay sini-synthesize bilang brickwork ng mga Givens rotation, at ang iisang-term na [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") ay nagiging iisang two-qubit na interaction gate.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because every fermionic gate here has a default synthesis, you can use the ready-made [`generate_preset_jw_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-jw-pass-manager#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager\") directly rather than hand-assembling the stages. Any keyword arguments are forwarded to the qubit stage; pass `optimization_level=0` for a faithful, unoptimized picture of the synthesized depth. Generating the full family of Krylov circuits is then a loop over the Krylov dimension. Keep the untranspiled [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\")s alongside the transpiled qubit circuits. The fermionic ones drive the exact (statevector) simulation in step 6, so they must stay measurement-free; `measure_all(inplace=False)` returns a measured copy to transpile and leaves the original untouched, and that copy is what a backend would execute.\n"
msgstr "Dahil may default na synthesis ang bawat fermionic gate dito, puwede mong gamitin nang direkta ang handa nang [`generate_preset_jw_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-jw-pass-manager#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager\") sa halip na i-assemble nang mano-mano ang mga stage. Ipinapasa sa qubit stage ang anumang keyword argument; ipasa ang `optimization_level=0` para sa tapat at hindi naka-optimize na larawan ng synthesized na depth. Ang pagbuo ng buong pamilya ng mga Krylov circuit ay isa na lang loop sa Krylov dimension. Itabi ang mga hindi pa na-transpile na [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") kasama ng mga na-transpile na qubit circuit. Ang mga fermionic ang nagpapatakbo ng exact (statevector) na simulation sa hakbang 6, kaya dapat manatili silang walang measurement; ang `measure_all(inplace=False)` ay nagbabalik ng kopyang may measurement na ita-transpile at hindi ginagalaw ang orihinal, at ang kopyang iyon ang isasagawa ng isang backend.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Krylov dimension shows up directly in the circuits’ two-qubit depth. The reference-state preparation is a fixed cost, and each additional Krylov power adds another second-order Trotter step of the time-evolution operator.\n"
msgstr "Direktang makikita ang Krylov dimension sa two-qubit depth ng mga circuit. Ang paghahanda ng reference state ay nakapirming gastos, at bawat karagdagang Krylov power ay nagdaragdag ng isa pang second-order na Trotter step ng time-evolution operator.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Splitting the Hamiltonian keeps these depths modest. The one-body evolution is a genuine orbital rotation, so it synthesizes to an [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate) brickwork on adjacent qubits. Each half step of the on-site interaction is a single [`RZZGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.RZZGate) coupling the impurity’s two spin modes; the cheap term that the second-order product sandwiches around the rotation. Handing the whole Hamiltonian to one [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate instead would Pauli-Trotterize the one-body part term by term, propagating long Jordan-Wigner `Z`-strings across the (long-range) impurity-bath couplings and inflating the depth by an order of magnitude.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Pinapanatiling katamtaman ng paghahati ng Hamiltonian ang mga depth na ito. Ang one-body evolution ay isang tunay na orbital rotation, kaya sini-synthesize ito bilang [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate) na brickwork sa magkakatabing qubit. Ang bawat kalahating hakbang ng on-site na interaksiyon ay iisang [`RZZGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.RZZGate) na nag-uugnay sa dalawang spin mode ng impurity; ang murang term na inilalagay ng second-order na product sa magkabilang gilid ng rotation. Kung ibibigay ang buong Hamiltonian sa iisang [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate, ite-Pauli-Trotterize nito ang one-body na bahagi bawat term, na magpapalaganap ng mahahabang Jordan-Wigner na `Z`-string sa (long-range) na mga impurity-bath coupling at magpapalobo ng depth nang isang order of magnitude.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The first circuit prepares only the reference determinant, while the last carries the most Trotter steps (four in this case):\n"
msgstr "Ang unang circuit ay naghahanda lang ng reference determinant, habang ang huli ang may pinakamaraming Trotter step (apat sa kasong ito):\n"

