msgstr "![A second-order Trotter Krylov circuit with four evolution steps.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/skqd-14.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"sample-bitstrings-from-the-krylov-circuits\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "6. Sample bitstrings from the Krylov circuits {#6-sample-bitstrings-from-the-krylov-circuits}"
msgstr "6. Mag-sample ng mga bitstring mula sa mga Krylov circuit {#6-sample-bitstrings-from-the-krylov-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "On hardware, you would run the transpiled circuits and measure. This is the noiseless (statevector) version of that step, showing the bitstrings SKQD would collect. Simulate each untranspiled [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") with [`ffsim.apply_unitary()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.apply_unitary.html#ffsim.apply_unitary \"(in ffsim)\") and sample the resulting statevector with [`ffsim.sample_state_vector()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.sample_state_vector.html#ffsim.sample_state_vector \"(in ffsim)\").\n"
msgstr "Sa hardware, patatakbuhin mo ang mga na-transpile na circuit at susukatin. Ito ang noiseless (statevector) na bersyon ng hakbang na iyon, na nagpapakita ng mga bitstring na kokolektahin ng SKQD. I-simulate ang bawat hindi pa na-transpile na [`FermionicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-fermionic-circuit#qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.FermionicCircuit\") gamit ang [`ffsim.apply_unitary()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.apply_unitary.html#ffsim.apply_unitary \"(in ffsim)\") at i-sample ang nagresultang statevector gamit ang [`ffsim.sample_state_vector()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.sample_state_vector.html#ffsim.sample_state_vector \"(in ffsim)\").\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") gate is validate-then-rotate under simulation (it checks that the incoming state occupies its reference determinant, then applies the rotation). Therefore, the input is the plain occupation determinant: the lowest `nocc` modes filled per spin, with no rotation. The gate applies `reference_rotation` itself.\n"
msgstr "Ang isang [`PrepareSlaterDeterminant`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-prepare-slater-determinant#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.PrepareSlaterDeterminant\") gate ay validate-then-rotate sa simulation (sinusuri nito na ang papasok na state ay sumasakop sa reference determinant nito, saka ina-apply ang rotation). Kaya, ang input ay ang payak na occupation determinant: ang pinakamababang `nocc` na mode ay puno kada spin, walang rotation. Ang gate mismo ang nag-a-apply ng `reference_rotation`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pooling the samples from all five Krylov circuits, the support is tiny: a few hundred distinct bitstrings out of the $\\binom{8}{4}^2 = 4900$ determinants in the `(4, 4)` sector. This concentration, a direct consequence of the momentum-basis sparsity established in step 2, makes the subsequent classical diagonalization tractable.\n"
msgstr "Kapag pinagsama ang mga sample mula sa lahat ng limang Krylov circuit, napakaliit ng support: ilang daang natatanging bitstring mula sa $\\binom{8}{4}^2 = 4900$ na determinant sa sector na `(4, 4)`. Ang konsentrasyong ito, direktang bunga ng momentum-basis sparsity na naitatag sa hakbang 2, ang nagpapadali sa susunod na klasikal na diagonalization.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Plotting the counts with [`qiskit.visualization.plot_histogram()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.visualization.plot_histogram) makes the sparsity visible. A few configurations dominate, led by the reference determinant.\n"
msgstr "Ang pag-plot ng mga count gamit ang [`qiskit.visualization.plot_histogram()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.visualization.plot_histogram) ay nagpapakita ng sparsity. Ilang configuration lang ang nangingibabaw, pangunahan ng reference determinant.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Histogram of the bitstrings sampled from the Krylov circuits, showing a small support.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/skqd-16.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Histogram of the bitstrings sampled from the Krylov circuits, showing a small support.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/skqd-16.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"diagonalize-in-the-sampled-subspace\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "7. Diagonalize in the sampled subspace {#7-diagonalize-in-the-sampled-subspace}"
msgstr "7. I-diagonalize sa sampled subspace {#7-diagonalize-in-the-sampled-subspace}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The sampled bitstrings are the input to the classical half of SKQD. The Hamiltonian is projected onto the subspace the sampled configurations span and diagonalized there. This is passed to the [qiskit-addon-sqd](/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd) package, whose [`diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian \"(in Sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD))\") runs the full sample-based quantum diagonalization loop. It builds a subspace from batches of the sampled configurations, diagonalizes the Hamiltonian in it, and iteratively refines the subspace by using configuration recovery: flipping occupations to repair configurations that violate the known particle-number symmetry. Configuration recovery is designed to undo the damage of hardware noise, which corrupts sampled bitstrings into the wrong particle-number sector; the sampling here is noiseless, so there is nothing to repair on that front.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga na-sample na bitstring ang input sa classical na bahagi ng SKQD. Ipo-project ang Hamiltonian sa subspace na sakop ng mga na-sample na configuration at doon ito dina-diagonalize. Ipinapasa ito sa package na [qiskit-addon-sqd](/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd), na ang [`diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian \"(in Sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD))\") ang nagpapatakbo ng buong sample-based quantum diagonalization loop. Bumubuo ito ng subspace mula sa mga batch ng mga na-sample na configuration, dina-diagonalize ang Hamiltonian doon, at paulit-ulit na pinapaganda ang subspace gamit ang configuration recovery: binabaligtad ang mga occupation para ayusin ang mga configuration na lumalabag sa kilalang particle-number symmetry. Ang configuration recovery ay idinisenyo para ayusin ang pinsala ng hardware noise, na nagpapasira sa mga na-sample na bitstring at inililipat ang mga ito sa maling particle-number sector; noiseless ang sampling dito, kaya walang kailangang ayusin sa aspetong iyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The solver consumes the sampled counts as a [`BitArray`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.BitArray), built directly from the pooled `counts` of step 6. Pass `num_bits` explicitly: without it, the width is inferred from the widest sampled bitstring, which is narrower than `2 * norb` whenever no sample occupies the last mode, and the solver then rejects the array. The solver diagonalizes in the same momentum basis the rest of the construction uses, so it takes the `h1e_momentum` and `h2e_momentum` integrals from step 2 directly, with no repacking. The recovered energy matches the exact reference to well under a milli-Hartree, from only a few hundred sampled configurations. Because the SQD energy is a variational upper bound on the true ground state, it always sits at or above `reference_energy` (still in scope from step 2):\n"
msgstr "Kinukuha ng solver ang mga na-sample na count bilang [`BitArray`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.primitives.BitArray), na direktang binuo mula sa pinagsamang `counts` ng step 6. Ipasa nang tahasan ang `num_bits`: kung wala ito, hinuhulaan ang lapad mula sa pinakamalapad na na-sample na bitstring, na mas makitid kaysa sa `2 * norb` kapag walang sample na sumasakop sa huling mode, at tatanggihan na ng solver ang array. Nagdi-diagonalize ang solver sa parehong momentum basis na ginagamit ng natitirang bahagi ng construction, kaya direkta nitong kinukuha ang mga integral na `h1e_momentum` at `h2e_momentum` mula sa step 2, nang walang repacking. Ang nabawing energy ay tumutugma sa eksaktong reference hanggang sa mas mababa pa sa isang milli-Hartree, mula lang sa ilang daang na-sample na configuration. Dahil ang SQD energy ay isang variational upper bound sa tunay na ground state, laging nasa o mas mataas ito sa `reference_energy` (nasa scope pa rin mula sa step 2):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Visualize the run: the energy’s convergence across the iterations, and the average occupancy of each spatial orbital in the recovered ground state. The per-iteration energy is the lowest across that iteration’s batches, and the occupancy sums the `orbital_occupancies` over the two spin sectors. Even without noise to correct, the energy decreases from iteration to iteration. Each iteration diagonalizes within `num_batches` batches of only `samples_per_batch` configurations subsampled from the pool, and the iterative refinement due to bitstring carryover steadily improves which configurations land in those batches, so the recovered energy improves:\n"
msgstr "I-visualize ang takbo: ang convergence ng energy sa bawat iteration, at ang average na occupancy ng bawat spatial orbital sa nabawing ground state. Ang energy kada iteration ay ang pinakamababa sa mga batch ng iteration na iyon, at pinagsasama ng occupancy ang `orbital_occupancies` sa dalawang spin sector. Kahit walang noise na itatama, bumababa ang energy sa bawat iteration. Nagdi-diagonalize ang bawat iteration sa loob ng `num_batches` batch na may `samples_per_batch` configuration lang na sinubsample mula sa pool, at ang paulit-ulit na refinement dahil sa bitstring carryover ay tuloy-tuloy na nagpapabuti kung aling mga configuration ang napupunta sa mga batch na iyon, kaya gumaganda ang nabawing energy:\n"

